.TH GLIMT 1 "2026-10-14" "Glimt 0.17.2" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
glimt \- fast, lightweight image viewer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B glimt
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.RI [ FILE_OR_FOLDER " ...]"
.br
.B glimt
.B \-\-remote
.I COMMAND
.br
.B glimt
.B \-\-remote\-all
.I COMMAND
.br
.B glimt
.B \-\-help
.br
.B glimt
.B \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Glimt
shows the images of a folder, one at a time, with a file list beside them. It is inspired by
.BR geeqie (1)
and uses its keyboard shortcuts, but focuses on speed and little memory: the images on each
side of the shown one are decoded in advance at window size, and folders with hundreds of
thousands of files list as quickly as small ones.
.PP
Given a file, Glimt shows it with the rest of its folder; given a folder, its first image;
given nothing, the folder used last (if that is set in Preferences) or the current folder.
Given several folders, Glimt shows the images of all of them as one list, for example for a
slideshow across them; random order mixes them all.
A URI such as
.I smb://server/share
is mounted with
.BR gio (1)
first.
.PP
It reads JPEG, PNG, WebP, GIF (also animated), TIFF (also with several pages) and camera RAW
files by their embedded preview. Builds with optional features also read videos, HEIC, AVIF,
JPEG XL and SVG.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-slideshow
Start the slideshow once the folder is read.
.TP
.B \-\-random
Show the slideshow in random order. Kept for later starts, as in the View menu.
.TP
.B \-\-fullscreen
Start in full screen.
.TP
.B \-\-kiosk
Full screen with only the image, for a picture screen: the keys and the mouse browse, zoom,
change the layout and run the slideshow, but there are no menus or panels, nothing changes
files or settings beyond these, and Escape, Q, Ctrl+Q and closing the window are refused.
Only
.B glimt \-\-remote quit
(or
.BR \-\-remote\-all )
ends it. The desktop's own keys (switching windows, logging out) still work; to keep them
away, run Glimt as the only program of a kiosk session, for example
.B cage \-\- glimt \-\-kiosk \-\-slideshow
.I ~/Pictures
or as the program of a GNOME Kiosk session.
.TP
.BI \-\-layout " LAYOUT"
Show several images at once, as View \(-> Layout:
.B 1
(one image),
.B 2x1
(side by side),
.B 1x2
(above each other) or
.B 2x2
(four). Kept for later starts.
.TP
.BI \-\-fade " off|short|long"
How the slideshow goes from one image to the next: at once, or fading over 0.4 or 1 second.
Kept for later starts.
.TP
.BI \-\-name " NAME"
Name this Glimt: letters, digits,
.B \-
and
.BR _ ,
not only digits. The window title shows it, and
.B glimt \-\-name
.I NAME
.B \-\-remote
.I COMMAND
sends
.I COMMAND
to this Glimt only (with
.BR open ,
it starts one with that name if none runs). A named Glimt listens even when remote
control is off in Preferences.
.TP
.BI \-\-remote " COMMAND"
Send
.I COMMAND
to the Glimt window used last.
.TP
.BI \-\-remote\-all " COMMAND"
Send
.I COMMAND
to every running Glimt.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
List the options and remote commands.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version.
.SH REMOTE COMMANDS
.TP
.BR next ", " prev ", " first ", " last
Show the next, previous, first or last image.
.TP
.B slideshow
Start or stop the slideshow.
.TP
.B random
Turn random order on or off.
.TP
.B fullscreen
Enter or leave full screen.
.TP
.BI open " PATH"
Show a file or folder. If no Glimt is running, one is started.
.TP
.B quit
Close Glimt.
.SH KEYS
The keys are Geeqie's; Help \(-> Keyboard Shortcuts lists them all, and Preferences can change
them. The most used:
.TP
.BR Space ", " "Page Down" ", " \(->
Next image.
.TP
.BR Backspace ", " "Page Up" ", " \(<-
Previous image.
.TP
.BR Home ", " End
First and last image.
.TP
.BR Z ", " X ", " + ", " \-
Zoom 1:1, zoom to fit, zoom in and out.
.TP
.BR F ", " F11 ", " Esc
Enter and leave full screen.
.TP
.BR S ", " P ", " R
Start or stop the slideshow, pause it, random order.
.TP
.BR ] ", " [
Rotate the view clockwise and counterclockwise.
.TP
.B Delete
Move the selected files, or the shown one, to the trash; in a collection, take them out of it.
.TP
.BR C ", " O
New collection of the selected files; open a collection.
.TP
.BR Ctrl+K ", " Alt+K
The EXIF panel, with the keywords and comment; Alt+K to edit the keywords.
.TP
.B Ctrl+P
Print the selected images, or the shown one, to a printer or a PDF file.
.TP
.B Shift+S
The sort manager: folders that the selected files are copied or moved to with a click.
.TP
.B Ctrl+J
Pan view: the images by day, as a timeline.
.TP
.B D
Find duplicates among the images in the list.
.TP
.B Ctrl+O
Preferences.
.TP
.B F1
Help.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/glimt/config
Preferences, as key=value lines (default
.IR ~/.config/glimt/config ).
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/glimt/sort-folders
The sort manager's folders, one on each line.
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/glimt/themes
Own themes, one
.I name.theme
file each, of
.I key=value
lines.
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/glimt/state
The last folder and the window size and position (default
.IR ~/.local/state/glimt/state ).
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/glimt/marks
Marks and stars, in builds with the marks feature.
.TP
.IB file .xmp
Keywords, comment and (if chosen) stars of
.IR file ,
next to it, read by darktable and digiKam too.
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/glimt/plugins
Plugins: desktop files whose command runs on the selected files (default
.IR ~/.local/share/glimt/plugins ).
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/glimt/collections
Collections, as Geeqie .gqv files (default
.IR ~/.local/share/glimt/collections ).
.TP
.I $XDG_CACHE_HOME/thumbnails
Thumbnails, shared with other programs as the freedesktop specification says.
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/glimt
The sockets for remote control.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.BR XDG_CONFIG_HOME ", " XDG_STATE_HOME ", " XDG_CACHE_HOME ", " XDG_DATA_HOME ", " XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
.BR XDG_CONFIG_HOME ", " XDG_STATE_HOME ", " XDG_DATA_HOME ", " XDG_CACHE_HOME ", " XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
Where the files above are kept.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B glimt ~/Pictures
Show the images in ~/Pictures.
.TP
.B glimt \-\-remote next
Go to the next image in the Glimt used last, for example from a desktop shortcut.
.TP
.B glimt \-\-remote\-all quit
Close every Glimt.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR geeqie (1),
.BR gio (1),
.BR lp (1),
.BR ffmpeg (1)
.PP
